        <http://imagoarchive.it/ilrmoo/R18_created>
                <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/douai/bibliothquemarcelinedesbordesvalmore/887/48r105r> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/oxford/corpuschristicollegelibrary/400/1r45v> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/leiden/universiteitsbibliotheek/b.p.l._13/61r113v> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/london/britishlibrary/harley_4003/3r37r> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/london/britishlibrary/royal_13.a.xiv/10v58v> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/dublin/trinitycollege/574/124r208v> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/cambridge/emmanuelcollegelibrary/i.1.3/87r120v> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/aberystwyth/nationallibraryofwales/3074d/159> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/cambridge/saintcatharinescollege/3_(e.iv.96)/105v167v> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/paris/bibliothquenationaledefrance/lat._4846/1r62v> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/dublin/nationallibraryofireland/700/1r48v> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/london/britishlibrary/claudius_e_viii/13v13v> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/cityofwestminsterlondon/westminsterabbeymuseum/23/169> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/london/britishlibrary/harley_3724/5r44r> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/london/britishlibrary/add._44922/77r105v> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/oxford/bodleianlibrary/tanner_2/151177> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/paris/bibliothquenationaledefrance/lat._4126/49r96v> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/cambridge/universitylibrary/mm.5.30/131> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/london/britishlibrary/add._33991/3r26r> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/london/britishlibrary/cotton_faustina_c_iv/155> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/cambridge/universitylibrary/mm.2.18/144v146v> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/paris/bibliothquenationaledefrance/lat._1111/1r27r> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/london/britishlibrary/add._34762/2r71v> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/london/britishlibrary/cotton_cleopatra_d.v/5r55r> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/london/lambethpalacelibrary/622/1r71v> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/london/collegeofarms/vincent_418/5r16v> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/cambridge/peterhousecollegelibrary/177_(1.8.1)/1r16r> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/london/britishlibrary/arundel_14/1r27v> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/cambridge/gonvilleandcaiuscollegelibrary/290/682/684693> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/london/britishlibrary/harley_359/68r125r> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/oxford/bodleianlibrary/_rawl._b._188/1r37v> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/oxford/bodleianlibrary/511_(s.c._2179)/190> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/cambridge/universitylibrary/ff._1._27/253r354r> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/london/britishlibrary/royal_13.b.viii/1r34v> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/oxford/bodleianlibrary/rawlinson_b._483_(s.c._11830)/136> , <https://imagoarchive.it/ontology/resources/manuscript/oxford/bodleianlibrary/laud_misc._720_(s.c._1062)/134v244r> ;
        :has_abstract  "La Topographia Hiberniae o Topographia Hibernica è un resoconto del territorio e una descrizione del popolo irlandese composta da Giraldo Cambrense tra il 1185 e il 1188, dopo l'invasione normanna dell'Irlanda. L'autore, nativo del Galles, si recò nell'isola una prima volta nel 1183 e una seconda nel 1185 insieme al principe Giovanni per ordine del re Enrico II. Il secondo viaggio durò dal 25 aprile 1185 alla Pasqua del 1186. L'opera è divisa in tre parti (distinctiones): la prima è relativa al paesaggio naturalistico irlandese, la seconda alle meraviglie dell'isola e la terza alla storia e cultura del popolo. La Topographia si presenta in cinque diverse redazioni, che si differenziano per aggiunte e revisioni compiute dallo stesso autore sul testo nel corso del tempo. " .

